NAME: fsverify
LAST DEPLOYED: Mon Oct 26 20:36:02 2026
NAMESPACE: fsverify
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 1
TEST SUITE: None
NOTES:
FlexaScale 0.4.0 installed as release "fsverify" in namespace fsverify.

Target application : namespace flexascale-bookstore, selector app.kubernetes.io/part-of=bookstore
Mode               : observe  (decisions are computed and logged; nothing is changed)
Prometheus         : http://monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus.flexascale-monitoring.svc:9090

1. Check the operator and the services it selected:
   kubectl -n fsverify logs deploy/fsverify-operator | head -40

2. Inspect proposed decisions (JSON lines, one per service per step):
   kubectl -n fsverify exec deploy/fsverify-operator -- tail -n 20 /var/log/flexascale/decisions.jsonl

3. Controller ownership:
   kubectl -n flexascale-bookstore get lease flexascale-bookstore
   kubectl -n flexascale-bookstore get hpa -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,MIN:.spec.minReplicas,MAX:.spec.maxReplicas,FROZEN_BY:.metadata.annotations.flexascale\.io/frozen-by

4. Enable live control only after reviewing step 2:
   helm upgrade fsverify <chart> -n fsverify --reuse-values --set policy.mode=live

Return control to native HPA at any time:
   helm upgrade fsverify <chart> -n fsverify --reuse-values --set policy.mode=observe
Uninstall (the operator restores frozen HPAs on shutdown; the application is not touched):
   helm uninstall fsverify -n fsverify
